{
"about":"Round 34: shape outlines both phones draw (ShapeGeometry.path) at the element's own size, from its base polygon in a 0…1 box times w and h, every vertex filleted with a circular arc of radius held to half the shorter adjacent edge, and its reach along each edge to half that edge too (the arc's radius taken down with it); a vertex where the outline runs straight on is not rounded. The path starts where the first vertex's arc leaves it (at the first vertex when it is not rounded), runs L to each next arc's start and A to its end (sweep 1 for a turn clockwise on the page, else 0), and closes. Numbers are to the hundredth, a whole number with no point. params outside their range are held to it (points and sides rounded to whole); absent ones take the shape's own. A speech bubble with no radius rounds by a tenth of its shorter side; a thought bubble is an ellipse (the top 70% of the box) and its tail, and takes no radius.",
